WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:16.347
The Earthworms stood at the entrance to the Willow Creek Cemetery.

2
00:00:16.348 --> 00:00:18.467
It had just stopped raining.

3
00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:22.509
Now the last drops dripped from the tree branches.

4
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:28.199
Gray fog drifted through the evening air and settled over the graves.

5
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.929
"Ooh," said Luke. "Spooky!"

6
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:41.032
"Yeah!" said Katie. "Like a scary movie! Waa-haa-haa!"

7
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:45.526
"Why didn't we come in the daytime?" asked AJ.

8
00:00:45.527 --> 00:00:53.225
"BECAUSE," said Emily, "in the daytime, we might run into another scavenger team."

9
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:59.023
"Now if there are no more questions, let's get busy," said Katie.

10
00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:03.566
"We have to check all the old graves."

11
00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.415
Emily looked at AJ.

12
00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:10.080
"Since you can't read, just sit on this bench and wait."

13
00:01:10.081 --> 00:01:14.846
AJ gulped. "By myself?"

14
00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:17.804
"You'll be our guard," said Luke.

15
00:01:17.805 --> 00:01:21.041
"Call us if you see anything strange."

16
00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:25.792
"Waa-haa-haa!" said Katie again.

17
00:01:25.793 --> 00:01:30.635
"And here—hold on to the bag," said Emily.

18
00:01:30.636 --> 00:01:37.403
"Wait," said AJ. But the three Earthworms disappeared in the fog.

19
00:01:37.404 --> 00:01:41.345
AJ shivered and sat down on the bench.

20
00:01:41.346 --> 00:01:44.223
He put the scavenger bag on his lap.

21
00:01:44.224 --> 00:01:46.854
He listened for voices.

22
00:01:46.855 --> 00:01:51.311
"Here's one from 1952." That was Emily.

23
00:01:51.312 --> 00:01:55.915
"Here's one from 1943." That was Luke.

24
00:01:55.916 --> 00:02:00.596
"1917." That was Katie.

25
00:02:00.597 --> 00:02:04.109
The voices floated further and further away.

26
00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.535
Then everything was still.

27
00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:11.785
Near the bench where AJ sat was a block of marble.

28
00:02:11.786 --> 00:02:15.589
AJ tipped his head back and looked up.

29
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:19.637
A gloomy marble lady stood on top of the block.

30
00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:23.812
She was looking straight down at AJ.

31
00:02:23.813 --> 00:02:27.803
"Mind your own business," said AJ.

32
00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:30.469
He moved to the other end of the bench.

33
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.167
He tapped his toes.

34
00:02:32.168 --> 00:02:35.266
He whistled a few notes.

35
00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:37.770
Then he slowly raised his head.

36
00:02:37.771 --> 00:02:42.552
The marble lady was staring right into his eyes.

37
00:02:42.553 --> 00:02:45.882
AJ shivered and looked away.

38
00:02:45.883 --> 00:02:49.931
"Why did they leave me alone?" he thought.

39
00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:52.202
"I'm an Earthworm too."

40
00:02:52.203 --> 00:02:55.193
Then he heard a voice.

41
00:02:55.194 --> 00:03:01.640
"AJ," it called. "AJ . . ."

42
00:03:01.641 --> 00:03:03.736
"Hello?"

43
00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:08.544
"Aaay-Jaay."

44
00:03:08.545 --> 00:03:12.174
"Who's there?" he whispered.

45
00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:15.599
"AJ! Over here! Bring the bag!"

46
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.577
AJ jumped to his feet.

47
00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:23.317
"Emily!" he shouted and ran down the pathway into the fog.

48
00:03:23.318 --> 00:03:29.553
He found the Earthworms at the edge of the cemetery near a dark grove of pine trees.

49
00:03:29.554 --> 00:03:33.216
They were gathered around an old gravestone.

50
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:38.694
"This is it—1859," said Katie.

51
00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:41.079
AJ stared at the stone.

52
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.314
"Now that we've found it, what do we do?

53
00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:47.129
Put it in our bag?"

54
00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.685
"HA!" said Katie.

55
00:03:49.686 --> 00:03:53.231
"No, silly," said Emily to her brother.

56
00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.918
"We make a crayon rubbing."

57
00:03:55.919 --> 00:03:58.546
"We better hurry," said Luke.

58
00:03:58.547 --> 00:04:01.540
"The sun is going down fast."

59
00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.591
Katie unrolled the paper.

60
00:04:03.592 --> 00:04:06.330
"Luke and AJ, hold the top."

61
00:04:06.331 --> 00:04:11.532
She held out her hand to Emily. "Crayon, please."

62
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:16.751
Katie placed the side of the crayon on the paper and began rubbing.

63
00:04:16.752 --> 00:04:20.053
The words on the gravestone began to appear:

64
00:04:20.054 --> 00:04:21.180
EMILY

65
00:04:21.181 --> 00:04:23.545
DEAR WIFE OF

66
00:04:23.546 --> 00:04:25.786
AJ looked over his shoulder.

67
00:04:25.787 --> 00:04:29.010
"Did you hear that?" he whispered.

68
00:04:29.011 --> 00:04:31.372
"There's something in the trees."

69
00:04:31.373 --> 00:04:34.326
The Earthworms listened.

70
00:04:34.327 --> 00:04:37.816
"I don't hear anything," said Emily.

71
00:04:37.817 --> 00:04:40.654
"Neither do I," said Katie.

72
00:04:40.655 --> 00:04:42.866
She rubbed some more.

73
00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:43.923
EMILY

74
00:04:43.924 --> 00:04:46.511
DEAR WIFE OF GEORGE WATSON

75
00:04:46.512 --> 00:04:47.663
DIED

76
00:04:47.664 --> 00:04:50.425
APRIL 29,

77
00:04:50.426 --> 00:04:53.288
"Now I hear it!" said Emily.

78
00:04:53.289 --> 00:04:57.407
"Something is moving in there!" Katie looked up.

79
00:04:57.408 --> 00:05:00.578
"It's laughing!" said Emily.

80
00:05:00.579 --> 00:05:04.662
"No—it's crying!" said Luke.

81
00:05:04.663 --> 00:05:09.130
"It's the marble lady!" screamed AJ.

82
00:05:09.131 --> 00:05:12.841
"WHO?" cried the Earthworms.

83
00:05:12.842 --> 00:05:18.066
"Never mind!" cried AJ. "Let's go, Katie!"

84
00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:23.307
"We have to finish!" said Luke. "We need the year!"

85
00:05:23.308 --> 00:05:27.472
Katie rubbed the crayon for the final time.

86
00:05:27.473 --> 00:05:28.507
EMILY

87
00:05:28.508 --> 00:05:30.744
DEAR WIFE OF GEORGE WATSON

88
00:05:30.745 --> 00:05:31.751
DIED

89
00:05:31.752 --> 00:05:35.904
APRIL 29, 1859

90
00:05:35.905 --> 00:05:40.945
"Got it!" cried Katie. "Let's get out of here!"

91
00:05:40.946 --> 00:05:45.958
The Earthworms ran, slipping and sliding on the wet grass.

92
00:05:45.959 --> 00:05:48.634
"The bag!" cried AJ.

93
00:05:48.635 --> 00:05:52.160
Emily ran back and grabbed the bag.

94
00:05:52.161 --> 00:05:55.684
"Wait for me!" she screamed.

95
00:05:55.685 --> 00:05:59.011
The Tornadoes jumped out of the pine grove.

96
00:05:59.012 --> 00:06:04.848
They were laughing their heads off.
